LIVE. Open TeleVuer on PICO at the Wi-Fi IP of this computer, port 8012.
Press right A with both sticks centred to arm; right B to disarm; Ctrl+C to exit.
STARTUP HOME: once PICO is ready, 3s countdown then slow joint-zero homing. B cancels.
Base is locked until homing finishes. Keep arms unloaded and path clear.
BASE + ARMS + WAIST. Release grips and centre both sticks before A. Hold each grip to move that arm.
Left Y requests arm homing; release grips/centre sticks; B cancels; A resumes after home.
Arm config: /home/unitree/Proj/Proj_PICO_G1-D/config/arms.json; speed=0.25 rad/s, bridge=0.3 rad/s, loop=20 Hz
DEX3: left/right index trigger controls each hand; grips continue to move arms.
Release both triggers before A; hands keep measured pose until trigger is used.
Right stick left/right turns the waist; arms and camera move with the torso.
Waist yaw: +/-30.0 deg, speed=0.1 rad/s; centre stick decelerates to hold.
Left X toggles right stick up/down: LIFT (default) <-> PITCH. Centre right stick after switching.
Waist pitch: [0.0, 30.0] deg, speed=0.08 rad/s; stick forward leans forward.
Column lift ENABLED: right stick up/down; feedback bounds [0.0, 0.42] m of rt/hispeed_state.y.
Lift directional stops: [0.010, 0.410] m; inward motion allowed in end margins.
B stops base/lift and holds arms/waist; Y homes only the 14 arm joints.
